            "issue": "The adversative relation expressed by “proof against superstition” is not established by the note’s appeal to an argumentative sense of πρός. δεισιδαιμονίας is genitive, not the accusative object of πρός; the overt accusative nominal group is τὴν ... πολλὴν ... ἀπόδειξιν. The relationship between that prepositional group and παρέχειν therefore needs an explicit account. The note’s alternatives “against” and “concerning” do not disclose this syntactic difficulty. This is an interpretive issue in the supplied image-checked wording, not evidence of an OCR error or grounds for inventing missing text.",
